{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["That your generations may know — its plain sense is like the words of those who say in tractate Sukkah: a literal sukkah. And this is its rationale: 'The festival of Sukkot you shall make for yourself when you gather from your threshing floor and from your winepress' — when you gather the produce of the land and your houses are full of every good thing, grain, wine, and oil. 'That you may remember' — 'that I made the children of Israel dwell in sukkot in the wilderness forty years' — with no settlement and no inheritance; and from this you shall give thanks to the one who gave you an inheritance and houses full of every good thing, and you shall not say in your hearts, 'My power and the might of my hand made me this wealth.' And in this very order it is found in the portion of Eikev: 'And you shall remember the whole way that YHWH your Elohim led you these forty years' etc., 'and He fed you the manna' etc. And why do I command you to do this? 'For YHWH your Elohim is bringing you to a good land' 'and you shall eat and be sated' 'and your heart grow haughty' 'and you forget YHWH' etc., 'and you say in your heart: My power and the might of my hand made me this wealth' 'and you shall remember YHWH your Elohim, that it is He who gives you power to make wealth.' Therefore they go out from houses full of every good thing at the time of gathering and sit in sukkot, as a remembrance that they had no inheritance in the wilderness and no houses to dwell in. And because of this rationale the Holy One, blessed be He, fixed the festival of Sukkot at the time of gathering of threshing floor and winepress, so that one's heart not grow haughty over houses full of every good thing, lest they say, 'Our hands made us this wealth.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:22.304075820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}